.IX Title "WebService::ILS::RecordedBooks 3pm"
.TH WebService::ILS::RecordedBooks 3pm "2026-06-25" "perl v5.32.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH "NAME"
WebService::ILS::RecordedBooks \- WebService::ILS module for RecordedBooks services
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 3
\&    use WebService::ILS::RecordedBooks::Partner;
\&    or
\&    use WebService::ILS::RecordedBooks::Patron;
.Ve
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
WebService::ILS::RecordedBooks::Partner \- services
that use partner credentials, for any patron
.PP
WebService::ILS::RecordedBooks::PartnerPatron \- same as above,
except it operates on a single patron account
.PP
WebService::ILS::RecordedBooks::Patron \- services
that use individual patron credentials, in addition to partner credentials
.PP
WebService::ILS::RecordedBooks::PartnerPatron is preferred over
WebService::ILS::RecordedBooks::Patron because the later requires patron
credentials \- username and password. However, if you do not know patron's
email or RecordedBooks id (barcode) you are stuck with Patron interface.
.PP
See WebService::ILS
.SH "CONSTRUCTOR"
.IX Header "CONSTRUCTOR"
.ie n .SS "new (%params_hash or $params_hashref)"
.el .SS "new (%params_hash or \f(CW$params_hashref\fP)"
.IX Subsection "new (%params_hash or $params_hashref)"
\fIAdditional constructor params:\fR
.IX Subsection "Additional constructor params:"
.ie n .IP """ssl""            => if set to true use https" 12
.el .IP "\f(CWssl\fR            => if set to true use https" 12
.IX Item "ssl => if set to true use https"
.PD 0
.ie n .IP """domain""         => RecordedBooks domain for title url" 12
.el .IP "\f(CWdomain\fR         => RecordedBooks domain for title url" 12
.IX Item "domain => RecordedBooks domain for title url"
.PD
.PP
\&\f(CW\*(C`client_id\*(C'\fR is either RecordedBooks id (barcode) or email
.PP
\&\f(CW\*(C`domain\*(C'\fR if set is either \*(L"whatever.rbdigital.com\*(R" or \*(L"whatever\*(R",
in which case rbdigital.com is appended.
